cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "sublift: incremental LTV measurement for subscription retention experiments"
message: "If you use sublift in work you publish, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: devjoinedthechat
    website: "https://github.com/devjoinedthechat"
repository-code: "https://github.com/devjoinedthechat/sublift"
abstract: >-
  sublift estimates the incremental lifetime value of a retention intervention
  from a randomized subscription experiment, over an explicit horizon of billing
  periods. It handles right-censored outcomes, models churn in discrete billing
  periods, separates voluntary from involuntary churn as competing risks, and
  provides anytime-valid confidence sequences so that interim monitoring does not
  inflate the false-positive rate.
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - survival analysis
  - experimentation
  - sequential testing
  - subscription
  - churn
  - customer lifetime value
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
